WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.020
Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker gave fans
plenty of answers to long-burning questions,

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.030
but it didn't end without leaving a few mysteries
unsolved, one of which involved two of the

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.660
sequel trilogy's most important characters.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.820
Major spoilers ahead for The Rise of Skywalker.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:19.210
In the last journey through the galaxy far,
far away within the Skywalker saga, Rey heads

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:24.650
out with Finn, Poe Dameron, Chewbacca, C-3PO,
and BB-8 in search of a Sith wayfinder, which

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:28.119
will guide them to the desert planet Exegol
within the Unknown Regions.

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:32.840
They encounter danger on the way as Kylo Ren
continues to Force-sense --and effectively

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:33.840
stalk - Rey.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.180
Following a lead on the planet of Pasaana,
the Resistance fighters race away in the general

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.730
direction of the long-forgotten ship of Sith
loyalist Ochi of Bestoon.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:46.960
Having barely managed to shake off the chasing
stormtroopers as they head out into the desert,

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.270
the group's speeders are ultimately hit and
blasted to pieces.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.540
Then, they all start to sink into a quicksand-like
substance.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.660
"Ahhh s---, quicksand.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.990
Ah dang, now we are in trouble."

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:04.500
Believing this may be his last moment before
death, Finn calls out to Rey, wanting to tell

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.219
her something important.

00:01:06.219 --> 00:01:08.520
Before he can say it, though, he sinks beneath
the sand.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.820
While Rey later asks Finn what he wanted to
say - and Poe tries throughout the rest of

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:17.249
the film to press the issue and uncover Finn's
secret - the former Stormtrooper brushes them

00:01:17.249 --> 00:01:21.649
off, leaving the audience without an answer
even after The Rise of Skywalker ends.

00:01:21.649 --> 00:01:22.820
What was he going to say?

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.710
He was sinking into the desert, so maybe he
just wanted to tell Rey how he didn't like

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:30.259
sand, because it's coarse and irritating and
it gets everywhere.

00:01:30.259 --> 00:01:32.149
Okay, probably not.

00:01:32.149 --> 00:01:36.259
The prevailing theory among fans seems to
be that Finn wanted to confess romantic feelings

00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:37.259
towards Rey.

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:42.229
However, Finn actor John Boyega took to Twitter
to refute that particular theory, writing:

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:43.229
"No...

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:45.930
Finn wasn't going to say I love you before
sinking!"

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:49.959
Realistically speaking, a romance between
Finn and Rey wouldn't have made much sense

00:01:49.959 --> 00:01:54.649
at all, with Finn and Rose Tico having a hint
of a romantic thing in The Last Jedi and with

00:01:54.649 --> 00:01:57.500
Rey and Kylo Ren experiencing a ton of emotional
tension.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.760
"Do you have something, a cowl or something
you could put on.”

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.180
With a ton of fan theories running rife, The
Rise of Skywalker co-writer and director J.J.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:15.470
Abrams decided to clear the air surrounding
Finn's big reveal that never actually came

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:16.920
to fruition in the film.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.420
According to Twitter user Kaila Ren, Abrams
revealed that Finn's secret is something astute

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.330
fans may already have guessed: Finn is Force-sensitive,
just like Rey.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.910
Ren posted in a tweet:

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:31.879
"JJ said it meant to him that he wanted to
tell Rey he was force sensitive, but purposely

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:33.290
left it open ended."

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:37.569
Games Radar also reported that Abrams added
the open-ended nature of Finn's secret so

00:02:37.569 --> 00:02:40.799
it, quote, "could mean different things to
different people."

00:02:40.799 --> 00:02:44.980
We're not entirely sure why this was a secret
that Poe wasn't allowed to know, but Finn

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:49.590
certainly wasn't going to share the info with
his Resistance co-General even with all his

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:50.590
ribbing.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.511
As we mentioned, Finn's Force-sensitivity
is something that's hinted at throughout the

00:02:53.511 --> 00:02:58.420
entire Star Wars sequel trilogy - but most
prominently throughout The Rise of Skywalker.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:02.000
In the film, he was be able to sense when
Rey was in danger, was somehow able to pick

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.189
out exactly which of the Star Destroyers of
the massive Final Order fleet was the command

00:03:06.189 --> 00:03:10.870
ship, and felt Rey briefly die after she defeated
Emperor Palpatine.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:15.319
Even before all that, Finn was able to break
free from the extensive brainwashing stormtroopers

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:19.610
are subjected to in the First Order, which
is something CinemaBlend points out as further

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:22.000
evidence of Finn's Force-sensitive nature.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.180
Overall, this is a much better explanation
than the fan-favorite one of Finn wanting

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.819
to confess his love for Rey, as it ties into
everything we know about Finn.

